   "headline": "Isaiah Joe and an 18-0 run carry Pistons past Magic",
   "story": "Orlando led 27-20 early in the second quarter before Detroit scored 18 straight points, and the Pistons went ahead for good at 28-27 during that run. Detroit led by as many as 18 in the third quarter and won by that margin, forcing 20 Orlando turnovers with 12 steals. Isaiah Joe scored 21 points with five threes, Daniss Jenkins had 15 points and 10 assists, and Ausar Thompson added 10 rebounds, seven assists and four blocks. Desmond Bane scored 21 and Franz Wagner 20 for Orlando, which was without Paolo Banchero, while Cade Cunningham did not play for Detroit.",
